  "term": "dorsal anterior cingulate cortex",
  "definition": "The dorsal anterior cingulate cortex (dACC) is a deeper cortical brain region that can be targeted in neuromodulation research. In the supplied source, it is the stimulation target being studied in schizophrenia to see whether changing activity in this area may help with negative symptoms and cognitive difficulties.",
